        "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    vector<vector<bool>> blockedCells(n, vector<bool>(n, false));\n    for (int c = 0; c < m; c++) {\n        int i, j;\n        cin >> i >> j;\n        blockedCells[i][j] = true;\n    }\n\n    vector<int> dp(n, 0);\n    if (!blockedCells[0][0]) dp[0] = 1;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n            if (blockedCells[i][j]) {\n                dp[j] = 0;\n            } else if (i != 0 || j != 0) {\n                int fromAbove = dp[j];\n                int fromLeft = (j == 0) ? 0 : dp[j - 1];\n                dp[j] = (fromAbove + fromLeft) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << dp[n - 1] << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n",
        "path": "src/solution.cpp"
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis": "A single-row dynamic program eliminates the per-row copy and second DP buffer while retaining O(N^2) work and exact modular results; fast iostream setup also reduces input overhead.",
    "notes": "Uses in-place row-major recurrence: dp[j] is the value from above before overwrite and dp[j-1] is the current-row value. Blocked cells reset the state, including blocked start/end.",
